Molotov Cocktail — Construction Guide

Materials:
- Glass bottle (wine/beer bottle, thick glass, completely dry, labels removed)
- Flammable liquid (gasoline standard; diesel burns longer and sticker)
- Motor oil (optional — 3:1 fuel-to-oil ratio for sticky flame; not required)
- Cotton rag (12–18 inch strip, torn from t-shirt works fine)
- Funnel (to pour fuel without spilling)
- Lighter or matches

Procedure:

1. Prepare the bottle
   - Use thick glass (wine or beer bottles work best)
   - Wash completely with hot water
   - Dry thoroughly — any water inside reduces flame intensity
   - Remove all plastic labels and stickers (they catch fire)

2. Fill with fuel
   - Use funnel to pour fuel into bottle
   - Fill 2/3 to 3/4 full (too full = spillage, too little = weak spread)
   - If using motor oil: add at 3:1 ratio (3 parts gasoline, 1 part oil) for stickier burn
   - Wipe any fuel spilled on bottle exterior

3. Prepare the wick
   - Cut cotton rag into 12–18 inch strip
   - Soak the entire rag in same fuel you're using
   - Roll tightly lengthwise so it fits snugly in bottle neck
   - Leave roughly half the rag inside the bottle (soaked in fuel), half outside (for lighting)

4. Assemble
   - Insert soaked rag into bottle opening
   - Bottom half sits submerged in fuel
   - Top half hangs outside bottle, ready to light

5. Deployment (when ready to use)
   - Soak exterior end of wick in fuel one more time
   - Light the wick immediately before throwing
   - Throw in arcing motion (underhand or overhand, about 40-degree angle)
   - Bottle breaks on impact, fuel disperses, wick ignites the spread

Physical Safety Notes:
- Do not light until ready to throw — burning bottles are dangerous to hold
- Fuel vapor inside the bottle is flammable — never shake or agitate the assembled device
- Keep fuel away from face and hands during construction; splashes burn
- Wear shoes and eye protection if available — glass shards on impact are hazard
- Never hold a lit bottle — throw immediately after ignition
- Store any unused fuel in sealed metal container, away from ignition sources, in cool area
- Cleanup: let any spilled fuel evaporate before working in the area

